# Alpha

This chapter declares its own `theorems:` block. There is no book-wide `theorems:` key
to inherit from (it was retired on 2026-08-02), so a chapter's counter policy is
entirely its own — and must not leak to a sibling chapter.

`shared:` puts theorem and lemma on ONE counter, and a book chapter scopes the number,
so these read "Theorem 1.1" and "Lemma 1.2".

::: {.theorem #thm-alpha title="Alpha"}
The first claim of the shared sequence.
:::

::: {.lemma #lem-alpha title="Alpha helper"}
The second, continuing the same counter rather than starting a new one.
:::
